Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Read-only answer for GUIs: why a player may not play a land

Forge's own GUIs simply leave a land unmarked when canPlayLand refuses
it (or show nothing after a click). A GUI that says why - not the
player's turn, not at sorcery speed, the land for this turn is played
already, an effect forbids it - needs Forge's own answer instead of
counting lands or reading card types itself:

- Player.landPlayRefusal(Card, boolean, SpellAbility): the reason
  canPlayLand refuses, or null. The checks of canPlayLand moved
  unchanged, in the same order, into landPlayRefusal; canPlayLand is
  landPlayRefusal == null. The limit (getMaxLandPlays, unlimited land
  plays) is Forge's as before.

No rule, card or AI behaviour changes: the new method only asks, and
the moved code runs as before.

Written for OpenMana on 2026-10-13.
---
 .../main/java/forge/game/player/Player.java   | 41 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/player/Player.java b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/player/Player.java
index 4cbb6de..ae8167f 100644
--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/player/Player.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/player/Player.java
@@ -1656,40 +1656,67 @@ public class Player extends GameEntity implements Comparable<Player> {
     }
 
     public final boolean canPlayLand(final Card land, final boolean ignoreZoneAndTiming, SpellAbility landSa) {
+        // OpenMana patch 0010 (2026-10-13): the checks moved unchanged, in the same order, into landPlayRefusal.
+        return landPlayRefusal(land, ignoreZoneAndTiming, landSa) == null;
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * OpenMana patch 0010 (2026-10-13): why this player may not play a land
+     * now. canPlayLand refuses exactly when this names a reason; its checks
+     * run here unchanged and in the same order, so a GUI can say why Forge
+     * does not offer a land instead of guessing.
+     */
+    public enum LandPlayRefusal {
+        /** CR 305.3: only during the player's own turn. */
+        NOT_YOUR_TURN,
+        /** Only when a sorcery could be cast (main phase, empty stack), unless the land may be played with flash. */
+        TIMING,
+        /** Another player's card without a permission to play it. */
+        NOT_OWNER,
+        /** Not from this zone (the battlefield, or another zone than the hand without a permission). */
+        ZONE,
+        /** A static ability forbids playing this land (CantBeCast). */
+        RESTRICTED,
+        /** The lands this player may play this turn are used up. */
+        LIMIT
+    }
+
+    /** OpenMana patch 0010 (2026-10-13): why canPlayLand(land, ignoreZoneAndTiming, landSa) refuses, or null if it does not. */
+    public final LandPlayRefusal landPlayRefusal(final Card land, final boolean ignoreZoneAndTiming, SpellAbility landSa) {
         if (!ignoreZoneAndTiming) {
             // CR 305.3
             if (!game.getPhaseHandler().isPlayerTurn(this)) {
-                return false;
+                return LandPlayRefusal.NOT_YOUR_TURN;
             }
             if (!canCastSorcery() && (landSa == null || !landSa.withFlash(land, this))) {
-                return false;
+                return LandPlayRefusal.TIMING;
             }
 
             final boolean mayPlay = landSa == null ? !land.mayPlay(this).isEmpty() : landSa.getMayPlay() != null;
             if (land.getOwner() != this && !mayPlay) {
-                return false;
+                return LandPlayRefusal.NOT_OWNER;
             }
 
             final Zone zone = game.getZoneOf(land);
             if (zone != null && (zone.is(ZoneType.Battlefield) || (!zone.is(ZoneType.Hand) && !mayPlay
                     && (landSa == null || !landSa.isAlternativeCost(AlternativeCost.Mayhem))))) {
-                return false;
+                return LandPlayRefusal.ZONE;
             }
         }
 
         // CantBeCast static abilities
         if (StaticAbilityCantBeCast.cantPlayLandAbility(landSa, land, this)) {
-            return false;
+            return LandPlayRefusal.RESTRICTED;
         }
 
         // **** Check for land play limit per turn ****
         // Dev Mode
         if (getMaxLandPlaysInfinite()) {
-            return true;
+            return null;
         }
 
         // check for adjusted max lands play per turn
-        return getLandsPlayedThisTurn() < getMaxLandPlays();
+        return getLandsPlayedThisTurn() < getMaxLandPlays() ? null : LandPlayRefusal.LIMIT;
     }
 
     public final int getMaxLandPlays() {
-- 
